Repair the MVX source issues exposed by warning-enabled GCC and Clang
builds: make kernel-doc complete, remove pseudo-kernel-doc comments and
dead locals, correct format strings, preserve error returns, and annotate
the driver's printf-like callbacks. Use strscpy() for the bounded video
device name now that Linux no longer provides in-kernel strncpy().

Also make the expected absence of debugfs a single debug-level notice.
Only install the RAM-drain reset callback after its debugfs-only state is
fully initialized, stop when interruptible locking fails, and propagate
drain construction failures through the existing unwind path.

